# drivers/TegraGM20BMetal on the host:
#   raw_target_test   raw/runtime/raw_target.h: the raw path's color target words, pitch as before and a mip chain's level as
#                     NVK's block-linear target, addressing every texel where raw/fx's layout (the texture header's and
#                     the 2D engine's view of the chain) has it
#   raw_layout_test   drivers/TegraGM20B/TegraGM20BLayout.h: the block-linear layout every GPU user takes is NIL's (its
#                     answers for one-level images of every texel size), raw/fx's level 0 and the display's tiled scan
#   raw_block_layout_test  raw/fx's block-compressed image (the no-copy texture layout) is NIL's, levels included, and its
#                     CPU copies put every byte where the block-linear addressing has it
#   nvk_wait_any_test nvkmd_darwin's WAIT_ANY (nvkmd_darwin_wait_any.h) over a model of the kext's WaitFence: it returns
#                     once one sync of the set resolves (a host signal, a fence's interrupt), sleeps until then, keeps
#                     its deadline, and calls a passed fence whose wake never came a lost interrupt
#   nvk_kill_test     nvkmd_darwin's view of a channel the kernel killed (nvkmd_darwin_kill.h): the fence word's kill record
#                     names the seqnos that never ran, a kept record answers for its old channel alone, a timeline keeps
#                     its failed values
#   nvk_surfaces_test nvkmd_darwin's ExecSurfaces record (nvkmd_darwin_surfaces.h): each BO once with its accesses merged,
#                     past its room the all-imports flag, its length
#   raw_events_source_test  how a command buffer with a plain or shared Metal event stays raw (frontend, bridge, m2v,
#                     RawMetal), and the cross-process shared event refusal line
#   raw_linked_source_test  how a render pipeline's linked functions reach m2v (frontend, bridge, its C and Rust forms)
#                     and how the raw path's twin and record key take them
#   raw_encode_profile_test  raw/runtime/raw_encode_profile.h: a debug build's encode spans count only inside an
#                     encode, each part's time holds its nested parts', and the totals fold profiles and keep the longest
#                     prepare
#   raw_follow_test   raw/runtime/raw_follow.h: the raw path's threads take a fixed-priority committer's policy, never a
#                     lower one, and keep their own for a timeshare committer
#   raw_slm_test      raw/runtime/raw_slm.h: the shader local memory a program's header or a kernel's QMD asks of a
#                     warp, the area NVK sizes for it, the methods that give it to the raw channel's 3D and compute
#                     classes (the runtime's, never a record's), ahead of every program of the pack or a record
#   raw_view_test     raw/runtime/raw_view.h: a kernel's texture slot binds the texture's own header, or a header of its
#                     memory with the word 0 of m2v's view of it in another format of the same texel size (a half
#                     texture's unsigned twin), with no sRGB conversion; texels of another size or blocks bind none
#   raw_tic_words_test  raw/runtime/raw_zeta.h and raw_gpu.cpp's block-compressed rows: each depth/stencil format's
#                     SET_ZT_FORMAT and texture header word 0, and each compressed format's word 0, rebuilt from NIL's
#                     row of NVK's format by NIL's generator rules
#   mkpack_owned_test raw/pack/mkpack.py: no blob or baseline register is one the raw path owns
#   splits_layout_test  raw/pack/splits.py: a split is packed only where its per-pixel program binds its uniform
#                     buffers as its whole program does
#   raw_tiled_cache_test  raw/runtime/raw_tiled_cache.h: with the kernel's tiled-cache bit, deko3d's configuration then the
#                     enable at context init and one flush per pass and per command buffer; nothing without it
#   raw_comp_test     raw/runtime/raw_comp.h: the compressible kinds the raw path binds are the kernel kind table's (nouveau
#                     gm200_mmu_kind) and demote as it says; the boot ZBC values read alike by Metal and NV format
#   stage_test        stage-tegra-gm20b-metal.py on a directory standing in for the Data volume
#   inventory_test    raw/test/inventory.tsv, selgaps.txt and refused.txt still describe the kinds' sent tables (selcover,
#                     over the host harness, writes them from the raw device's objects)
#   rawpack_records_test  what the pack generator keeps of a probe: texture3d entries, 32 set-0 entries and m2v's
#                     own buffer beside an 8-bit sRGB target
#   raw_ycbcr_test    raw/runtime/raw_ycbcr.cpp: the two-plane YCbCr textures the raw path converts (m2v's rules) and the
#                     conversion's shape; its texels against Metal's reads are raw/test/ycbcroracle.mm's (this Mac's GPU)
#   raw_xr_test       raw/runtime/raw_xr.h: the extended-range formats the raw path keeps and the codes Metal's Clear
#                     stores in them (an M4 Max's); against Metal's own reads and clears it is raw/test/xroracle.mm's
#   raw_clear_test    raw/runtime/raw_clear.h: the clear values the raw path hands NVK, m2v's for every format it renders
#                     (raw/test/targetcheck.py: its target formats against NVK's)
#   raw_sampler_test  raw/runtime/raw_sampler.h: the Metal samplers the raw path takes, as m2v samples them on NVK
#                     (raw/test/samplercheck: their headers against NVK's)
#   raw_archive_test  raw/runtime/raw_archive.h: the binary archive files the device opens where m2v's reader does not
#                     (iOS 27's thin Apple GPU binaries), as Metal opens a file of another GPU's binaries
#   raw_heap_test     raw/runtime/raw_heap.h: an MTLHeap's placements in its one span, Metal's contract (a full heap
#                     answers nil, aliasable ranges are taken again, usedSize and maxAvailableSizeWithAlignment)
#   raw_residual_test raw/runtime/raw_residual.h: a buffer bound off m2v's descriptor base alignment (16 bytes for a
#                     storage buffer, 256 for a uniform one) at the aligned base with its SlotBindOffset residual in the
#                     push word raw/pack/probe_bind.h's bind-offset run names
#   raw_cache_test    raw/runtime/raw_cache.h: the records the runtime makes for states and kernels the pack lacks, kept
#                     on disk and made once per process (raw/test/cachecheck: the same checks on a bucket's real records),
#                     and raw_metallib.h: the functions' AIR hashes that key them
#   raw_native_seed_test  raw/runtime/raw_cache.h's installed native records, packed (kits/SwitchSeedPack) and read in
#                     place; SWITCH_SEED_TREE=<an image's ngpu/addons> (--test_env) also reads back some of a built seed's
#   raw_bounds_test   raw/runtime/raw_bounds.h: a Core Animation draw's pixel box and rectangle from its vertices (against
#                     a GPU's coverage it is raw/test/boundsoracle.mm's, this Mac's GPU), and raw_region.h: the fetch
#                     barrier's region test over such draws, and which covers a render area (a clear it makes redundant)
#   raw_overlap_test  raw/runtime/raw_overlap.h: a fetching draw's triangles in runs that share no pixel (against a GPU's
#                     coverage it is raw/test/overlaporacle.mm's, this Mac's GPU)
#   raw_storage_form_test  raw/runtime/raw_storage_form.h, raw_key_tally.h: which attachments a storage form's views
#                     fit (compression tags, never Metal's compression flag), and the refusing keys' tally
#   raw_fetch_order_test  raw/runtime/raw_fetch_order.h: the fetching draws refused as they are recorded (their encoder
#                     alone goes to m2v) and those left to the CPU's geometry at submission
#   raw_record_samplers_test  raw/runtime/raw_record.h: a record's constexpr entries index its own sampler headers whoever
#                     made it (runtime, native seed), and the device places each header, the pack's first, once
#   nak_half_round_test  NAK's rewrites of metal2vulkan's half emulation (nak_nir_algebraic.py): its rounding as two
#                     conversions, the same for every f32 input; half sums and products in f32 as HADD2/HMUL2, the
#                     same for every pair of halves; and fquantize2f16's widening as HADD2.F32 (nak/from_nir.rs)
#   raw_order_test    raw/runtime/raw_order.h: the raw path orders on the CPU only after the kernel refused an Order, never
#                     while its channel is being made again, and orders on the GPU again once the kernel made it
#   raw_handler_order_test  raw/runtime/raw_handler_order.h: a queue's completed handlers run in the order its command
#                     buffers were enqueued, however the threads that finish them race
#   raw_scheduled_wait_test  raw/runtime/raw_scheduled_wait.h: waitUntilScheduled waits out a compile its queue's head
#                     waits for and wakes when it fails; only a shared-event wait lets it return before the submission
#   raw_replay_twins_test  raw/runtime/raw_replay_twins.h: a range m2v replays fails whole, before any pass of it is
#                     encoded, when an attachment of one of its passes has no twin
#   nak_fp32_flush_test  NAK's fp32 flush elision (nak_nir_algebraic.py): a flushed source under fneg or fabs feeds an FTZ
#                     instruction as its source does, and no FTZ result or widened half is a denormal
#
#   bazel test //drivers/TegraGM20BMetal/test:all
